  "scope": "Whole Federer 3.2.37, pp. 273--274: actual upper, lower and common Minkowski contents over the full positive real radius domain; nonnegative order, empty and closure laws; the whole-radius actual projection-volume lower bound; actual finite compact-family Gross supremum on Borel sources and arbitrary-original-source Gross comparison. Retain every admissible natural degree and ambient dimension, empty/nonmeasurable/unbounded sources, zero normal blocks and infinite values. Both degree-zero contents are counting measure; positive degrees fail the countable-cover measure law on an actual countable dense source.",
  "proof_route": "Actual unions of open metric balls give empty and closure tube laws and agree with every independently specified nonempty-source distance. Existing sealed extended bounds give the full radius limits. Adapted actual orthogonal coordinates and the outer-section Fubini bound identify whole normal balls before cancelling the positive normalization. Finite compact separation and finite additivity bound actual projected-family costs. Independent compact-family laws precede the proved Gross supremum. Existing Suslin parametrizations, opaque pruning, compact coordinate boxes, finite target-ball restrictions and radial exhaustion prove compact-source image approximation. Compact detection and finite original Borel partition approximation with one total error give the full 2.10.8 characterization. Closure restores arbitrary original sources. Exact finite disjoint-ball volume and arbitrary finite subsums prove degree-zero counting equality. Actual natural-power limits give positive-degree finite-source nullity; countable dense sources have whole-space infinite tubes and violate the countable-cover law.",
